# WA-FIXALL S6 stealth5 extras — battery fake power_supply + sim.state carrier.
# Companion facts recorded in images/gms-mtg-oemprop-stealth5/build-record.md.
#
# R59 battery EXTRA skin (S4 risk-ledger: BatteryManager EXTRA_* = Long.MIN
# sentinel because redroid /sys/class/power_supply is empty and the AIDL
# example health HAL reads healthd sysfs paths — "batteryPath not found").
# Fix = static fake psy directory bind-mounted over the empty sysfs dir at
# post-fs-data, BEFORE class hal/health service probes battery paths.
# Init builtin mount is fail-soft: if the mount fails the image default
# (empty dir, sentinel EXTRA) is preserved — no regression.
# Values are model-level consumer-phone story (NOT per-identity; identity
# battery level story stays in the BatteryService dumpsys-override layer).
#
# R42 detail: gsm.sim.state — telephony is present (gsm template) but no SIM
# ever registers, so the prop stays empty on redroid (real no-SIM consumer
# phone = "ABSENT"). One boot_completed setprop; measured: nothing else
# writes the prop afterwards.

# S6 v5 measured fix: init's mount builtin is `mount <fs> <node> <device>
# [options]` — node is the MOUNTPOINT and options is ONE arg (a 5th arg
# parses as numeric flags). v1-v4 had the paths swapped and "none bind"
# split across the options/flags slots, so the line failed and the sentinel
# survived (measured: no bind in mount table; real host-kernel psy files
# present with empty values = the Long.MIN root cause confirmed on-device).
on post-fs-data
    mount none /sys/class/power_supply/battery /vendor/etc/health-fake/battery bind

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    setprop gsm.sim.state ABSENT
